# Groovy version and extensions

The plugin runs Groovy hook and selector scripts with Groovy ${groovyVersion}. Groovy 4.0.33 added the Java 26 and 27
bytecode levels ([GROOVY-12200](https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/GROOVY-12200)), so scripts also run when Maven
runs on JDK 27. The plugin depends on these Groovy modules:

- `org.apache.groovy:groovy:${groovyVersion}`
- `org.apache.groovy:groovy-json:${groovyVersion}`
- `org.apache.groovy:groovy-nio:${groovyVersion}`, since 3.11.0: `java.nio.file.Path` extension methods such as
  `path.text` and `path.readLines()`
- `org.apache.groovy:groovy-xml:${groovyVersion}`

If your scripts (`setup`, `prebuild`, `postbuild`, `selector`) need another Groovy module, add it as a dependency of
the plugin, with the same version as the Groovy modules above, for example:

```xml
<project>
  <build>
    <plugins>
      <plugin>
        <artifactId>maven-invoker-plugin</artifactId>
        <version>${project.version}</version>
        <dependencies>
          <dependency>
            <groupId>org.apache.groovy</groupId>
            <artifactId>groovy-yaml</artifactId>
            <version>${groovyVersion}</version>
          </dependency>
        </dependencies>
      </plugin>
    </plugins>
  </build>
</project>
```

Older plugin versions shipped other Groovy versions, so an extension has to match the plugin version you use:

|Plugin version|Groovy|Group ID of the modules|
|:---|:---|:---|
|3.4.0 and later|Groovy 4|`org.apache.groovy`|
|3.3.0|Groovy 3|`org.codehaus.groovy`|
|before 3.3.0|Groovy 2, as `groovy-all`|`org.codehaus.groovy`|
